            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn't find it too sweet with just the two tablespoons of honey. I did add more chopped green onion. I made this last night and let the pork chops sit overnight in the marinade. We all enjoyed this, there were no leftovers. If I were to make this again, I'd add just a little more honey and garlic."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "April Nicholson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this recipe. Marinated pork chops for 2 hours but I did a dry rub prior to grilling to kick it up a notch prior to the grill. I did brown sugar, 5 spice, ginger, garlic and sesame seeds. It brought out the flavor! So good",
            "datePublished": "2020-03-05T00:41:01.627Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nancy C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Added 1/2 tsp Chinese Five-Spice to meat before adding marinade, as well as a sliced onion. Marinated overnight. Delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2020-10-18T01:49:30.873Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dana Todd"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I like more of an \"umami\" flavor so I add 2 T of fish sauce and reduce the honey. If you have never tried it, you will be amazed at how addictive it makes the final dish, much more complex and delicious especially for boring chicken. I have made this several times, and usually tinker with the ratio of onion, garlic and ginger. I've also found I can use chopped or mashed-ginger that comes in a jar, it tastes fine and if I'm in a hurry it's so much easier than grating fresh ginger or if you don't have any on hand. I usually omit the sesame seeds but it's good either way. I've also tried a spicier version, throwing in some red pepper flakes or chiles.",
            "datePublished": "2017-07-12T22:25:20.147Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jeraldo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I put in less honey but it was divine. Unfortunately, I cooked it at too high a temperature so the sauce in the bottom of the roasting pan burned a bit. I'll try a rack and water in the bottom next time.",
            "datePublished": "2018-09-26T01:11:05.473Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ShaunaLee7"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I tried marinating deer steak in this. I made it with no sweetener and additional 1/3 c oil. It made the best stir fry ever. I chopped my entire three inch piece of ginger and 4 cloves of garlic...wasn't too spicy. Excellent!",
            "datePublished": "2010-12-10T04:38:19.917Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "just_jam"
            },
            "reviewBody": "this turned out pretty tasty.. i used this on 3 thighs and 2 drumsticks and marinated for 8 hours.. to my surprise i only had 1 T of sesame oil left and no rice vinegar so i used what i had on hand.. the 1 T and subbed white wine vinegar.. i followed homschlrmom's modifications of using a 3 inch piece of ginger and 4 cloves of garlic.. i left out the honey and sesame seeds and totally forgot the pepper (doh!).. we cooked this on the grill (basting all the way through) and totally enjoyed the final product.. ty for the recipe",
            "datePublished": "2016-03-26T12:02:49.153Z"
          },
